quality.prompt:
Review this diff from a first-time external contributor:

```diff
+// Retry up to 3 times with a 500ms delay if the upstream call fails.
+// Added a test for the retry-exhaustion path since it wasn't covered before.
+async function fetchWithRetry(url, attempts = 3) {
+  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
+    try {
+      return await fetch(url);
+    } catch (e) {
+      if (i === attempts - 1) throw e;
+      await sleep(500);
+    }
+  }
+}
```

One issue I noticed myself: this doesn't distinguish a 4xx from a 5xx/network error, so it'll retry even on a request that will never succeed (e.g. a 400).
